WEBVTT

00:00.520 --> 00:04.050
What I want to do in this video
is find the area of this region

00:04.050 --> 00:07.200
that I'm shading in yellow.

00:07.200 --> 00:11.140
And what might seem challenging
is that throughout this region,

00:11.140 --> 00:12.810
I have the same lower function.

00:12.810 --> 00:14.540
Or I guess the
lower boundary is y

00:14.540 --> 00:16.870
is equal to x squared
over 4 minus 1.

00:16.870 --> 00:19.242
But I have a different
upper boundary.

00:19.242 --> 00:20.700
And the way that
we can tackle this

00:20.700 --> 00:23.290
is by dividing this
area into two sections,

00:23.290 --> 00:26.640
or dividing this region into two
regions, the region on the left

00:26.640 --> 00:28.250
and the region on
the right, where

00:28.250 --> 00:30.730
for this first region,
which I'll do--

00:30.730 --> 00:34.310
I'll color even more in
yellow-- for this first region,

00:34.310 --> 00:35.950
over that entire interval in x.

00:35.950 --> 00:40.360
And it looks like x is
going between 0 and 1.

00:40.360 --> 00:44.280
y equals-- when x is equal to
1, this function is equal to 1.

00:44.280 --> 00:47.220
When x is equal to 1, this
function is also equal to 1.

00:47.220 --> 00:48.810
So this is the point 1 comma 1.

00:48.810 --> 00:50.320
That's where they intersect.

00:50.320 --> 00:53.250
So for this section, this
subregion right over here,

00:53.250 --> 00:57.420
y equals square root of x is the
upper function the entire time.

00:57.420 --> 00:59.230
And then we can have
a-- we can set up

00:59.230 --> 01:02.860
a different-- we can
separately tackle figuring out

01:02.860 --> 01:04.920
the area of this region.

01:04.920 --> 01:07.960
From x is equal to 1
to x is equal to 2,

01:07.960 --> 01:10.890
where y equals 2 minus
x, is the upper function.

01:10.890 --> 01:12.450
So let's do it.

01:12.450 --> 01:14.710
So let's first think
about this first region.

01:14.710 --> 01:17.050
Well, that's going to be
the definite integral from x

01:17.050 --> 01:19.640
is equal to 0 to
x is equal to 1.

01:19.640 --> 01:25.120
And our upper function is square
root of x, so square root of x.

01:25.120 --> 01:28.390
And then from that, we want to
subtract our lower function--

01:28.390 --> 01:32.320
square root of x minus x
squared over 4 minus 1.

01:39.200 --> 01:42.400
And then of course,
we have our dx.

01:42.400 --> 01:46.350
So this right over here, this is
describing the area in yellow.

01:46.350 --> 01:49.730
And you could imagine it, that
this part right over here,

01:49.730 --> 01:51.660
the difference between
these two functions

01:51.660 --> 01:53.164
is essentially this height.

01:53.164 --> 01:54.580
Let me do it in a
different color.

01:57.820 --> 01:59.680
And then you
multiply it times dx.

01:59.680 --> 02:03.390
You get a little
rectangle with width dx.

02:03.390 --> 02:06.600
And then you do that for each x.

02:06.600 --> 02:08.860
Each x you get a
different rectangle.

02:08.860 --> 02:10.650
And then you sum them all up.

02:10.650 --> 02:14.570
And you take the limit as
your change in x approaches 0.

02:14.570 --> 02:16.664
So as you get ultra,
ultra thin rectangles,

02:16.664 --> 02:18.330
and you have an
infinite number of them.

02:18.330 --> 02:21.060
And that's our definition,
or the Riemann definition

02:21.060 --> 02:22.820
of what a definite integral is.

02:22.820 --> 02:25.370
And so this is the area
of the left region.

02:25.370 --> 02:27.370
And by the exact same
logic, we could figure out

02:27.370 --> 02:28.972
the area of the right region.

02:28.972 --> 02:30.680
The right region--
and then we could just

02:30.680 --> 02:32.127
sum the two things together.

02:32.127 --> 02:34.210
The right region, we're
going from x is equal to 0

02:34.210 --> 02:38.530
to x-- sorry, x is equal to
1 to x is equal to 2, 1 to 2.

02:38.530 --> 02:42.130
The upper function is 2 minus x.

02:42.130 --> 02:47.220
And from that, we're going to
subtract the lower function,

02:47.220 --> 02:49.660
which is x squared
over 4 minus 1.

02:53.780 --> 02:56.060
And now we just
have to evaluate.

02:56.060 --> 02:58.800
So let's first simplify
this right over here.

02:58.800 --> 03:02.100
This is equal to the
definite integral

03:02.100 --> 03:09.220
from 0 to 1 of square root of x
minus x squared over 4 plus 1,

03:09.220 --> 03:12.020
dx-- I'm going to write
it all in one color now--

03:12.020 --> 03:18.710
plus the definite integral
from 1 to 2 of 2 minus x,

03:18.710 --> 03:21.330
minus x squared over 4.

03:21.330 --> 03:25.330
Then subtracting a negative is
a positive 3-- or a positive 1.

03:25.330 --> 03:26.650
We could just add it to this 2.

03:26.650 --> 03:29.330
And so this 2 just becomes a 3.

03:29.330 --> 03:34.747
I said 2 minus
negative 1 is 3, dx.

03:34.747 --> 03:36.705
And now we just have to
take the antiderivative

03:36.705 --> 03:39.310
and evaluate it at 1 and 0.

03:39.310 --> 03:42.130
So the antiderivative
of this is-- well,

03:42.130 --> 03:43.480
this is x to the 1/2.

03:43.480 --> 03:44.730
Increment it by 1.

03:44.730 --> 03:47.500
Increment the power by
1, you get x to the 3/2,

03:47.500 --> 03:49.200
and then multiply
by the reciprocal

03:49.200 --> 03:53.650
of the new exponent-- so
it's 2/3 x to the 3/2.

03:53.650 --> 03:56.410
Minus-- the antiderivative
of x squared over 4

03:56.410 --> 04:02.160
is x to the third, divided by 3,
divided by 4, so divided by 12,

04:02.160 --> 04:03.660
plus x.

04:03.660 --> 04:05.510
That's the antiderivative of 1.

04:05.510 --> 04:09.590
We're going to
evaluate it at 1 and 0.

04:09.590 --> 04:11.640
And then here the
antiderivative is

04:11.640 --> 04:19.670
going to be 3x minus x
squared over 2 minus x

04:19.670 --> 04:22.029
to the third over 12.

04:22.029 --> 04:24.450
Once again, evaluate it
at-- or not once again.

04:24.450 --> 04:28.460
Now we're going to
evaluate at 2 and 1.

04:28.460 --> 04:30.610
So over here, you evaluate
all of this stuff at 1.

04:30.610 --> 04:35.690
You get 2/3 minus 1/12 plus 1.

04:35.690 --> 04:38.410
And then from that, you
subtract this evaluated at 0.

04:38.410 --> 04:41.010
But this is just all
0, so you get nothing.

04:41.010 --> 04:44.260
So this is what the yellow
stuff simplified to.

04:44.260 --> 04:46.740
And then this purple stuff,
or this magenta stuff,

04:46.740 --> 04:51.070
or mauve, or whatever color this
is, first you evaluate it at 2.

04:51.070 --> 04:58.330
You get 6 minus-- let's see,
2 squared over 2 is 2, minus 8

04:58.330 --> 04:58.920
over 12.

05:01.520 --> 05:03.650
And then from that,
you're going to subtract

05:03.650 --> 05:05.460
this evaluated at 1.

05:05.460 --> 05:13.270
So it's going to be 3 times 1--
that's 3-- minus 1/2 minus 1

05:13.270 --> 05:14.604
over 12.

05:14.604 --> 05:16.270
And now what we're
essentially left with

05:16.270 --> 05:17.889
is adding a bunch of fractions.

05:17.889 --> 05:19.180
So let's see if we can do that.

05:19.180 --> 05:20.930
It looks like 12 would
be the most obvious

05:20.930 --> 05:22.300
common denominator.

05:22.300 --> 05:29.430
So here you have 8/12
minus 1/12 plus 12/12.

05:29.430 --> 05:31.310
So this simplifies
to-- what's this?

05:31.310 --> 05:36.440
This is 19/12, the part
that we have in yellow.

05:36.440 --> 05:40.190
And then this business,
let me do it in this color.

05:40.190 --> 05:43.280
So 6 minus 2, this is
just going to be 4.

05:43.280 --> 05:51.100
So we can write this as
48/12-- that's 4-- minus 8/12.

05:51.100 --> 05:54.460
And then we're going to have to
subtract a 3, which is 36/12.

05:57.170 --> 06:02.410
Then we're going to add to
1/2, which is just plus 6/12,

06:02.410 --> 06:06.030
and then we're
going to add a 1/12.

06:06.030 --> 06:10.730
So this is all going to simplify
to-- let's see, 48 minus 8

06:10.730 --> 06:18.410
is 40, minus 36 is 4, plus
6 is 10, plus 1 is 11.

06:18.410 --> 06:21.614
So this becomes plus 11/12.

06:21.614 --> 06:23.030
Let me make sure
I did that right.

06:23.030 --> 06:28.830
48 minus 8 is 40,
minus 36 is 4, 10, 11.

06:28.830 --> 06:30.040
So that looks right.

06:30.040 --> 06:31.955
And then we're ready
to add these two.

06:31.955 --> 06:36.010
19 plus 11 is equal to 30/12.

06:36.010 --> 06:38.290
Or if we want to simplify
this a little bit,

06:38.290 --> 06:40.990
we can divide the numerator
and the denominator by 6.

06:40.990 --> 06:44.960
This is equal to
5/2, or 2 and 1/2.

06:44.960 --> 06:45.630
And we're done.

06:45.630 --> 06:50.560
We figured out the area
of this entire region.

06:50.560 --> 06:53.255
It is 2 and 1/2.
